      "source_file": "src/sqllens/safety/readonly.py",
      "claim_text": "_strip_leading_comments treats # as a line comment when dialect is None too, while sqlglot's default tokenizer does not; '#x\\nSHOW TABLES' with no dialect classifies as introspection (fails closed).",
      "skip_category": "uncategorized",
      "original_severity": "minor",
      "evidence": "The fix-delta inner re-fix cap (2 attempts) was spent with this finding open. It fails closed (a result is withheld, never admitted). With no dialect the classifier deliberately counts every engine's catalogs, so treating # as a comment under None follows the same union rule. The docstring wording '(and # on MySQL)' is the remaining mismatch."
    }
